What:           /sys/class/leds/*:rgb:joystick_rings/effect
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        Linux input mailing list <linux-input@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
                Select the AYANEO controller firmware LED effect. Reading
                returns the selected effect name. Supported writes are:

                none: standard multicolour brightness/intensity and the
                LED pattern trigger control the rings.

                rainbow: firmware cycles both rings through colours at a
                fixed speed. Brightness controls amplitude; zero turns the
                output off without changing the selected effect. Firmware
                controls hue and tempo, independently of multi_intensity.

                The rainbow effect requires no LED trigger to be selected.
                Hardware pattern writes fail with EBUSY while rainbow is
                selected. Select none before configuring a hardware pattern.
                Clearing the effect restores normal multicolour interpretation
                using the current brightness and cached intensity.

What:           /sys/class/leds/*:rgb:joystick_rings/effect_index
Date:           September 2026
Contact:        Linux input mailing list <linux-input@vger.kernel.org>
Description:
                Read-only, space-separated supported effect names:
                "none rainbow". The effect interface does not expose controller
                reset, module eject or arbitrary HID commands.
